# FinCalc Implementation Plan

FinCalc is a full-stack financial calculator suite and daily income/expense tracker. This plan details the architecture, page flows, data schema, and development workflow.

---

## Architecture & Directory Structure

To separate concerns cleanly, we will structure the repository into `/client` and `/server`:

```
/ (root)
├── package.json              # Runs dev/build command concurrently
├── client/                   # Vite + React app
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/       # Shared & calculator-specific components
│   │   ├── pages/            # Home, Calculators, Tracker, Dashboard, History, Login, Signup
│   │   ├── lib/              # Supabase JS client
│   │   ├── contexts/         # AuthContext (state, profiles, hooks)
│   │   ├── index.css         # Styling, premium dark/light themes
│   │   └── App.jsx           # Main router & theme provider
│   ├── vite.config.js
│   └── package.json
└── server/                   # Node.js + Express API
    ├── server.js             # Main server logic with Supabase Service Role Key integration
    └── package.json
```

---

## Database Schema (Supabase Postgres)

We will configure two main tables on Supabase with RLS enabled:

### `calculations`
Stores saved calculation logs for registered users.
- `id`: `uuid` PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT `gen_random_uuid()`
- `user_id`: `uuid` REFERENCES `auth.users` ON DELETE CASCADE NOT NULL
- `type`: `text` NOT NULL (e.g., 'emi', 'sip', 'compound', 'simple', 'amortization', 'retirement')
- `inputs`: `jsonb` NOT NULL (e.g., principal, interest rate, duration)
- `result`: `jsonb` NOT NULL (e.g., calculated values, monthly breakdowns)
- `created_at`: `timestamp with time zone` DEFAULT `now()`

### `transactions`
Stores daily income and expense entries.
- `id`: `uuid` PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT `gen_random_uuid()`
- `user_id`: `uuid` REFERENCES `auth.users` ON DELETE CASCADE NOT NULL
- `type`: `text` CHECK (`type` IN ('income', 'expense')) NOT NULL
- `category`: `text` NOT NULL
- `amount`: `numeric` NOT NULL
- `note`: `text`
- `date`: `date` NOT NULL DEFAULT `CURRENT_DATE`
- `created_at`: `timestamp with time zone` DEFAULT `now()`

